        ("Ambitious", "Sentimental", "I’m always thinking about the next goal, the next opportunity, the next version of my life. I’m also keeping the card, the photo, the receipt, and probably the random little thing you gave me six years ago."),
        ("Social", "Introspective", "I can talk to basically anyone. Big on small talk. Then I’ll go home and overthink the conversation, analyze the person, and wonder why humans are the way they are."),
        ("Decisive", "Indecisive", "Ask me which dress, restaurant, font, or shade of pink is better and I have an answer immediately. Ask me one major life question and suddenly I need a committee, seventeen tabs, and 3–5 business days."),
        ("Habitual", "Spontaneous", "Same hot vanilla latte every day. Same favorite colors. Same few foods on repeat. New restaurant tonight? Absolutely. Chicago in four hours? Apparently we’re going to Chicago."),
        ("Independent", "Attached", "I want my own career, my own interests, my own opinions, and a life that is completely mine. I also get ridiculously attached to my people and care about my relationships more than almost anything."),
        ("Techy", "Traditional", "I’m fascinated by AI, emerging technology, and whatever comes next. I’m equally fascinated by traditions that have survived for generations and why people still choose to carry them forward."),
        ("Sensitive", "Direct", "Please phrase my feedback gently. Yours is coming with sharp bullet points. I know, the irony is not lost on me. I’m working on meeting somewhere in the middle."),
        ("Polished", "Unfiltered", "I’ll edit the work seventeen times. My hair will be perfectly curled. My words? Considerably less edited. Perfectionism applies to the output, not always the commentary.")
    };
}
<section class="duality" id="duality">
    <div class="about-container">
        <h2 class="duality-title">The Duality of a Woman™</h2>
        <p class="kn-hint">Tap a card to see what I mean.</p>
        <div class="kn-carousel">
        <button type="button" class="kn-arrow kn-prev" aria-label="Previous cards">‹</button>
        <ul class="kn-cards">
            @for (var i = 0; i < dualities.Length; i++)
            {
                var (one, other, story) = dualities[i];
                <li class="kn-item n@(i % 4)">
                    <button type="button" class="kn-card" aria-pressed="false">
                        <span class="kn-inner">
                            <span class="kn-face kn-front dp-front">
                                <span class="dp-one">@one</span>
                                <span class="dp-and">and</span>
                                <span class="dp-other">@other</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="kn-face kn-back">@story</span>
                        </span>
                    </button>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
        <button type="button" class="kn-arrow kn-next" aria-label="Next cards">›</button>
        </div>
        @* the paragraph wraps up Duality and sets up the quiz beside it (stacks on phones) *@
        <div class="duality-row">
            <p class="duality-note">For a long time, I thought these things were supposed to add up more neatly. <strong>Now I think the contradictions are the point.</strong> I don’t fit perfectly into one category, and I don’t particularly want to.</p>
            <div class="quiz-col">
                @* the setup before the quiz: you've read the whole site, so here's the pop quiz *@
                <div class="quiz-intro">
                    <p class="quiz-intro-lead">Well, you’ve made it this far.</p>
                    <p>You’ve read about my work, my degree, my projects, my hobbies, and probably more of my personality than you expected when you opened this website.</p>
                    <p>Might as well find out if you retained any of it.</p>
                    <p><b>Pop quiz. Ten questions. No notes.</b></p>
                    <p class="quiz-intro-aside">This is mildly embarrassing if you get a 2.</p>
                </div>
                <h3 class="tot-title">How Well Do You Know Me?</h3>
                <p class="kn-hint">This or that? Guess my pick.</p>

                @* the quiz (built by the script below); the grid underneath is the no-JavaScript version *@
                <div class="quiz" id="quiz" data-questions="@Json.Serialize(thisOrThat.Select(t => new { a = t.Item1, b = t.Item2, pick = t.Item3, right = t.Item4, wrongA = t.Item5, wrongB = t.Item6, reveal = t.Item7 })).ToString()"
                     data-verdicts="@Json.Serialize(quizVerdicts).ToString()"
                     data-leaders="@Json.Serialize(quizLeaders.Select(l => new { name = l.Item1, score = l.Item2 })).ToString()" hidden>
                    <div class="quiz-card">
                        @* a quiz sheet: the header band, one step per question, then the question *@
                        <div class="quiz-top">
                            <span class="quiz-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
                            <span class="quiz-tally" aria-live="polite">Score 0</span>
                        </div>
                        <ol class="quiz-steps" aria-hidden="true"></ol>
                        <div class="quiz-play">
                            <p class="quiz-qnum"></p>
                            <p class="quiz-question"></p>
                            <div class="quiz-options" role="group" aria-label="Your guess"></div>
                            <p class="quiz-result-chip" aria-live="polite"></p>
                            <div aria-live="polite">
                                <p class="quiz-line"></p>
                                <p class="quiz-reveal"></p>
                            </div>
                            <button type="button" class="quiz-btn quiz-next" hidden>Next</button>
                        </div>
                        <div class="quiz-result" hidden>
                            <p class="quiz-score" aria-live="polite"></p>
                            <p class="quiz-verdict"></p>
                            <div class="quiz-verdict-body"></div>
                            <p class="quiz-rank"></p>
                            <div class="quiz-end-actions">
                                <button type="button" class="quiz-btn quiz-show-board" aria-expanded="false">View leaderboard</button>
                                <button type="button" class="quiz-btn quiz-again ghost">Play again</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="quiz-board">
                    <p class="quiz-board-title">Leaderboard ✦</p>
                    <ol>
                        @foreach (var (name, points) in quizLeaders)
                        {
                            <li><span>@name</span><b>@points/10</b></li>
                        }
                    </ol>
                    <div class="quiz-end-actions">
                        <button type="button" class="quiz-btn quiz-board-back ghost" hidden>‹ Back</button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <ul class="tot-grid">
                    @foreach (var (one, other, pick, _, _, _, reveal) in thisOrThat)
                    {
                        <li class="tot-card">
                            <span class="tot-pair">
                                <span class="tot-option@(pick == one ? " picked" : "")">@one</span>
                                <span class="tot-or">or</span>
                                <span class="tot-option@(pick == other ? " picked" : "")">@other</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="visually-hidden">My pick: @pick.</span>
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(reveal))
                            {
                                <span class="tot-line">@reveal</span>
                            }
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
